---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout>
	<section class="mb-5">
		<h1>PIXEL CO2</h1>
		<p class="text-xl bg-[#EEE8E0] px-2">POST-TREATMENT INSTRUCTIONS</p>
	</section>
	<section>
		<div class="separation">
			<h2>Congratulations!</h2>
			<p>Today your received your CO2 treatment/ Pixel Peel</p>
			<p>Please read these instructions to fully understand your treatment plan.</p>
			<p>Below are your post treatment care instructions.</p>
			<p>Your post-treatment care is vital to proper skin healing and ultimate results of the procedure. For best results, please follow these instructions. New skin will re-surface in 3-5 days. Wound care as detailed below should be followed until the skin has healed.</p>
		</div>

		<div class="separation">
			<h2>Days 1-3</h2>
			<p>What to expect: Redness, swelling (especially around the eyes), rough sandpaper-like texture, burning, mild oozing, itching, sensation of tightness, contact dermatitis and crusting. It is also possible to have reactivation of herpes simplex. These reactions, while sometimes alarming to patients, are normal and expected.</p>
			<p>	1. Take medications as prescribed ( Valtrex 500mg twice a day) if you have a history of cold sore (HSV1/2) <br>
				2. Sleep with your head elevated to minimize swelling. Ice packs can be used for discomfort and to reduce swelling. <br>
				3. Avoid strenuous activity, avoid saunas, jacuzzi, hot tubs, hot showers 1-2 weeks <br>
				4. Avoid direct sunlight at all times. If you have to go outside, use physical blockers such as hats, scarves, and sunglasses during this time period. <br>
				5. For Fitz skin types IV-V Hydrocortisone 1% post treatment may be indicated starting on day 7. <br>
			</p>
		</div>

		<div class="separation">
			<h2>Post CO2 laser treatment protocol</h2>
			<p>Please do not apply any other skin products that are not listed below, as other products may affect your wound healing process.</p>
		</div>

		<div class="separation">
			<h2>Immediately After Procedure:</h2>
			<h2>Night 1</h2>
			<p>	1. Alastin Gentle Cleanser <br>
				2. Puracyn Plus Spray <br>
				3. Alastin Regenerating Skin Nectar <br>
				4. Elta MD Moisture seal <br>
			</p>
		</div>

		<div class="separation">
			<h2>Day 2-14</h2>
			<h2>Morning (AM) Routine</h2>
			<p>	1. Alastin Gentle Cleanser <br>
				2. Puracyn Plus spray (discontinue after day 7) <br>
				3. Alastin Regenerating Skin Nectar <br>
				4. Elta MD Moisture Seal <br>
				5. UV Skin sunscreen (Not necessary if you stay indoors for the first week post-treatment) <br>
			</p>
			<h2>Night (PM) Routine</h2>
			<p>	1. Alastin Gentle Cleanser <br>
				2. Puracyn Plus Spray (discontinue after day 7) <br>
				3. Alastin Regenerating Skin Nectar. <br>
				4. Elta MD Moisture Seal <br>
			</p>
		</div>

		<div class="separation">
			<h2>Day 15</h2>
			<h2>Morning (AM) Routine</h2>
			<p>	1. Alastin Gentle Cleanser <br>
				2. Alastin Regenerating Skin Nectar <br>
				3. Elta MD restore moisturizer <br>
				4. UV Skin sunscreen <br>
			</p>
			<h2>Night (PM) Routine</h2>
			<p>	1. Alastin Gentle Cleanser <br>
				2. Alastin Regenerating Skin Nectar <br>
				3. Elta MD restore moisturizer <br>
			</p>
		</div>

		<div class="separation">
			<h2>Post-Treatment Recovery Tips</h2>
		</div>

		<div class="separation">
			<h2>Wound Care &amp; Hydration</h2>
			<p>	• Puracyn Plus Spray: Apply throughout the day as needed (typically 3–5 times daily during healing). <br>
				• EltaMD Moisture Seal: Apply generously whenever the skin feels dry, tight, or uncomfortable. <br>
			</p>
		</div>

		<div class="separation">
			<h2>Sun Protection</h2>
			<p>	• Avoid direct sun exposure during recovery. <br>
				• Wear a wide-brimmed hat when outdoors. <br>
				• After the first week, begin Mineral SPF 50 sunscreen and reapply every 2–3 hours when outside. <br>
			</p>
		</div>

		<div class="separation">
			<h2>Follow-Up Appointments</h2>
			<p>	• 2-Day Follow-Up: Healing assessment and skin evaluation. <br>
				• 2-Week Follow-Up: Progress review, skincare adjustments, and discussion of maintenance treatments for collagen remodeling. <br>
			</p>
		</div>

		<div class="separation">
			<h2>Comfort Measures</h2>
			<p>	• Tylenol® (Acetaminophen) 500mg may be taken every 6–8 hours as needed unless otherwise directed by your physician. <br>
			</p>
		</div>

		<div class="separation">
			<h2>Resuming Skincare Products</h2>
			<p>Retin-A, retinol products, AHA/BHA exfoliants, glycolic acid, salicylic acid, and other exfoliating products should not be resumed until cleared by your provider. Most patients wait approximately 4 weeks.</p>
		</div>

		<div class="separation">
			<h2>Makeup &amp; Exfoliation</h2>
			<p>	• Resume makeup only after complete skin healing and provider clearance. <br>
				• Avoid all exfoliating products and treatments for a minimum of 4 weeks. <br>
			</p>
		</div>

		<div class="separation">
			<h2>When to Contact kiwiMEDSPA</h2>
			<p>Contact us immediately if you experience increasing pain, excessive swelling, fever, worsening redness, yellow drainage, or any concern regarding your recovery.</p>
		</div>
	</section>
</Layout>
